---
title: Crispy Soft Shell Crabs with Thai Sweet Chilli Sauce
servings: 4
course: Starter
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Medium
prep time: 15m
cook time: 4m
tags:
- seafood
- savoury
- starter
---

Heat deep fat fryer to 190°C.

Make the batter by mixing the @flour{80%g}, @cornflour{40%g}, @salt{0.5%tsp}, @baking soda{2%tsp}, @ground turmeric{1%tsp}, @ground coriander{1%tsp}, and @ground black pepper{0.5%tsp}. Whisk in enough water to make a matter with the consistency of stirred soured cream.

Dip the @soft shell-crabs{4}(cleaned and prepared) in the batter, making sure that the entire body is covered, and gently drop them in the oil. Deep fry for 3 to ~{4%minutes} per side.

Remove the crabs from the oil and drain them on a paper towel-lined plate.

Serve with @Thai sweet chilli sauce{}.